WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.495
Idea. A sports shop buys a football for ten dollars and sells it for fifteen dollars. The five dollars it adds on top of the cost is its profit on each ball.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:19.038
Markup shows that profit as a percentage of the cost. Five divided by ten, times one hundred, is fifty per cent.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:32.722
Method. Step one: find the cost and the selling price. Step two: profit per unit is the price minus the cost. Step three: divide by the cost, and multiply by one hundred.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:43.795
Some questions run backwards. To find the price, multiply the cost by one plus the markup. To find the cost, divide the price by one plus the markup.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:59.334
Step five: round as asked, usually to two decimal places, and add the per cent sign. Markup can be over one hundred per cent. A four dollar item sold for ten has a markup of one hundred and fifty per cent.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:17.695
Worked example. Here is a real exam question from November 2020, Paper one. A drum kit costs one hundred and ninety pounds and sells for three hundred and fifty pounds. Calculate, to two decimal places, the markup. It is worth two marks.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:26.173
First the profit on each drum kit. Three hundred and fifty minus one hundred and ninety is one hundred and sixty pounds.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:40.764
Now divide by the cost. One hundred and sixty divided by one hundred and ninety, times one hundred, is eighty-four point two one zero. To two decimal places, eighty-four point two one per cent.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:47.967
Common mistake. The most common mistake is dividing by the selling price instead of the cost.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:55.110
When working backwards, do not take the percentage off the price. Divide by one plus the markup instead.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:08.473
Your turn. Now you try. A bakery sells a birthday cake for thirty-six dollars. Its markup is twenty per cent. Calculate the cost of making the cake. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:17.914
Answer. Cost equals price divided by one plus the markup. Thirty-six divided by one point two is thirty dollars.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:27.513
Check it. Thirty times one point two is thirty-six. Taking twenty per cent off thirty-six would give twenty-eight dollars eighty, which is wrong.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:42.275
Remember the method: profit is price minus cost, divide by the cost and multiply by one hundred. To work backwards, multiply or divide by one plus the markup. Now try the practice questions.
